      "object": "Although Murray et al.17 argue in favour of classifying muscle dysmorphia as an eating disorder, the Eating Attitudes Test, which is an instrument for assessing DE, may not be sensitive to the assessment of eating behaviors typical of individuals with a high drive for muscularity (patients with muscle dysmorphia). Thus, future research should use sensitive instruments to assess these behaviors. Furthermore, some intervening variables related to DE were not evaluated, such as ethnicity, psychological dependence on exercise and socioeconomic level."
